===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[decorated]] cloth hung at the back of a stage.
# An [[image]] that serves as a [[visual]] [[background]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 11, 2006|author=Sheryl Gay Stolberg
|title=Bush Mourns 9/11 at Ground Zero as N.Y. Remembers
|work=New York Times
|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2006/09/11/nyregion/nyregionspecial3/11bush.html?hp&ex=1158033600&en=e468f88da52557ed&ei=5094&partner=homepage
|passage=The president spoke outside the brick exterior of the firehouse for Ladder Company 10 and Engine Company 10, against the '''backdrop''' of a 56-foot-long bronze bas-relief depicting the towers in flames.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Guy W. Lecky-Thompson|title=Video Game Design Revealed|page=12|passage=Animated, seemingly varied crowd movement will place a game in the early 1990s, while static crowd '''backdrops''' and blocky, sprite-based athletes tend to point toward technology used in the 1980s.}}
# The [[setting]] or [[background]] of an [[act]]ed [[performance]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=May 9, 2012
|author=John Percy
|title=Birmingham City 2 Blackpool 2 (2-3 on agg): match report
|work=the Telegraph
|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/competitions/championship/9254026/Birmingham-City-2-Blackpool-2-2-3-on-agg-match-report.html
|page=
|passage=Blackpool’s aggregate victory ensures Birmingham are now preparing for a potential summer of change. Manager Chris Hughton has been operating against a '''backdrop''' of financial uncertainty all season and last night Peter Pannu, the vice-chairman, announced that the club’s accounts would finally be published next week, and that a new investor had been identified.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=European Court of Human Rights|title=M. M. v. The United Kingdom|section=marginal 171|issue=24029/07|date=13-11-2012|url=http://hudoc.echr.coe.int/eng?i=001-114517|passage=Specifically on the question of Article 8 considerations, the Court of Appeal expressed the view that it was difficult to see how a chief constable’s decision to disclose [the applicant’s charges to the employer] could ever be challenged (see paragraph 81 above). The Court observes that the case was decided against the '''backdrop''' of a clearly-defined legislative framework (i.e., the 1997 Act, which was in force in England and Wales at the time) which the court took to be in compliance with Article 8 (see paragraph 78 above).}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 6, 2016
|author=James Zogby
|title=Israel’s prickliness blocks the long quest for peace
|work=The National
|url=http://www.thenational.ae/opinion/comment/israels-prickliness-blocks-the-long-quest-for-peace#full
|page=
|passage=All of this heightened hyper-reaction to criticism plays out against a '''backdrop''' of dangerous moves by Israel and its supporters in the US to not only defame and politically punish critics and in some instances to go further by making criticism illegal.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Any background situation.
#: {{ux|en|Against a '''backdrop''' of falling interest rates, the new savings account is looking less appealing.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|author=Philip Haigh|title=RDG lauches voluntary redundancy scheme|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=9|text=Against this '''backdrop''', RDG said it needed to "review historic working practices so that the railway can respond to changing passenger needs and enable future growth".}}

